      "abstractNote": "This software repository provides an approach for exploring and evaluating literature-based document-to-document (doc-2-doc) recommendations using the FastText model. It leverages the FastText model to first generate word embeddings and then generates document embeddings by centroid aggregation of the word embeddings. It utilizes the RELISH Corpus, a biomedical literature dataset curated by experts, containing pairwise document assessments.\n\nThe software workflow includes training FastText models on a predefined training set, followed by the evaluation of doc-2-doc recommendations using a distinct test set. Additionally, Optuna is integrated for hyperparameter optimization of the trained FastText models using the validation dataset, enabling fine-tuning of model performance.",
